  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-12> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-12--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-12--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2023-glue-12: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.67" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.669"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.81"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The bacterial intervention and head-number outcome are concrete and can have strong causal controls. Public availability of animal-level records is uncertain, and the manipulative 'hijack' framing is not required by the phenotype." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare head-number outcomes in germ-reduced planaria colonized with the candidate commensal, vehicle controls, and heat-killed or mutant bacteria, then test clearance and re-colonization rescue. Increased two-headed regeneration attributable to live bacteria confirms the experimental result." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Matched microbiome and morphology data may not be public.", "Antibiotic or colonization procedures can independently alter regeneration.", "Override and hijack imply function beyond causation." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2023-glue-12--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2023-glue-12--gpt--dataset-2> .
